he wealthiest  men in North America to help you take  your business to new riches here are  three action items that you can learn  from chillicothe action Adam number one  lead from the front your business will  only be as strong as the people you have  helping you if you want them to perform  and be motivated than you need to be a  source of inspiration and lead them  after a particularly rough year in 1974  when inflation rates rose unexpectedly  chick-fil-a was hit hard in the  pocketbook they had to spend more money  on advertising to track people into the  restaurants not wanting his operators to  lose their shirts Cathy decided he would  cover the unexpected increase in costs  he took the hit so they wouldn't have to  according to kathy i didn't take a  salary that year because i didn't want  our employees to take pay cuts I  struggled with this but I was determined  not to lose sleep over it too many CEOs  are leaving sinking ships they should be  the last ones to leave the company if  some people are losing money everybody  should lose money not just the  stockholders action item number to build  a culture if you're really clear about  the type of company that you want to  build and the type of people that you  want to hire then it will be much easier  to attract people to you who believe in  your vision there's no right or wrong  culture but it's important that you  build one that people can rally behind  if you really want to accelerate your  business growth Cathy doesn't believe  that businesses should be open seven  days per week he built a culture around  working hard for six days and then  having one day off to spend with your  family and for your spiritual well-being  as a result he attracts people who  believe in that culture and strengthen  it according to cathy why do we closed  on Sunday well it started back in  nineteen forty six when I opened my  first restaurant after the first week I  determined that if it took seven days a  week to make a living I should be in  some other business we find closing on  Sunday attracts those people who give  attention to spiritual growth and our  family oriented the fact that we have  sunday closing helps attract quality  employees  action Adam number three keep your  priorities in order as entrepreneurs we  often don't do a great job of managing  our lives we work too hard eat bad food  don't look after our bodies neglect  those around us all in the name of  building our businesses if that's you it  might be time to reconsider where your  priorities are when Kathy with 38 years  old who is diagnosed with colon cancer  he thought his life as he knew it was  over it wasn't but the experience did  force Kathy to re-examine his principles  according to kathy i think i'd like to  be remembered as one who kept my  priorities in the right order we live in  a changing world but we need to be  reminded that the most important things  will not change if we keep our  priorities in the proper order  so remember lead from the front build a  culture and keep your priorities in  order the finish of this video I wanted  to share one of my favorite true stories  about truett Cathy and some of his  basketball as chick-fil-a group Cathy  knew he needed a new tactic to attract  more customers this was one Cathy first  introduced advertising hiring a company  to give chick-fil-a a public face the  result large billboards showing cows  that urge people to eat more chicken it  was a humorous slogan and it worked  thank you for joining me for another  edition of all the Masters I hope you  enjoyed if you like the video please  give it a thumbs up I'd also love to  hear your thoughts and comments if you  want to leave it below and stay tuned  for the next episode  you
 

